WEBVTT

00:00:00.008 --> 00:00:06.672
When reading a common table expression query, do not read top to bottom as one giant statement.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:10.637
First understand the common table expression by itself.

00:00:10.637 --> 00:00:14.507
Then ask what the final query does with that stage.

00:00:14.507 --> 00:00:17.972
Here the common table expression filters patients.

00:00:17.972 --> 00:00:21.372
The final query joins admissions and aggregates.

00:00:21.372 --> 00:00:26.671
This staged reading style is one reason common table expressions improve clarity.
